 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to licenses to sell liquors at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S2009",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2009-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64-a, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2009               REVISED 03/17/11\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to licenses to\nsell liquors at retail for consumption on certain premises\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill would allow the business establishment Gran Piatto d'Oro to\nobtain a liquor license.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nThis bill amends the Alcoholic Beverage control Law, allowing issuance\nof a retail license for on-premises consumption of alcohol for a\npremises within 200 feet of a place of worship, provided that the\npurpose of such premises is for the sale and consumption of food or\nbeverage, and such premises is within the boundaries of the borough\nof Manhattan as directed therein.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nWhile the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law prohibits the sale for\non-premises consumption of alcohol at any location within 200 feet of\na place of worship, exceptions have been made for certain\nestablishments that do not pose problems for the place of worship, or\nthe surrounding neighborhood. This bill would exempt Gran Piatto\nd'Oro. in New York City from this provision of law thereby allowing\nsale and consumption of alcohol in the restaurant.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2009-10: Referred to Commerce, Economic Development & Small Business\n2009-10: Passed Senate\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
